#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059422 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/id #uuid "e95210c5-adb4-519e-bbec-e240dac32fd8" :question/math-academy-id "e-3614" :question/problem "Write $2\\sin{15^\\circ} \\cos{15^\\circ}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=15^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin 15^{∘}\\cos 15^{∘} &= \\sin (2 \\cdot 15^{∘}) = \\sin 30^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059423 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/id #uuid "35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3618" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{24})\\cos (\\frac{π}{24})]\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\n$$\n\nwe can further simplify the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[2\\sin (\\frac{π}{12})\\cos (\\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[\\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{12})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\sin (\\frac{π}{6}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059424 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/id #uuid "b03496ac-c3b2-5d65-a3e3-2a33ea0cb862" :question/math-academy-id "e-3619" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\dfrac{\\sin 25^\\circ}{\\sin 50^\\circ}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin{2x} = 2\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=25^\\circ$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\sin\\left(2\\cdot 25^\\circ\\right) = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\sin 50^\\circ = 2\\sin 25^\\circ \\cos 25^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the ${\\color{blue} \\sin 50^\\circ}$ in the denominator as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{\\sin 50^{∘}} &= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sin 25^{∘}}{2\\sin 25^{∘}\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2\\cos 25^{∘}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\sec 25^{∘}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059425 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "539b5b86-7b31-52c9-be04-e80d6799b68a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3623" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $3\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}$." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac {\\pi}{8}\n$$\n\ninto the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\sin (2 \\cdot \\frac{π}{8}) \\\\\n&= \\sin (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2\\sin \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) \\cos \\left(\\dfrac {\\pi} {8} \\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the above by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 2\n$$\n\ngives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\sin (\\frac{π}{8})\\cos (\\frac{π}{8}) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\, {\\color{black}\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{8}\\right)}} = 3 \\left(\\color{black} \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\right) = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4483a191-ab5f-53cc-9a25-631101495ec5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256212} {:answer/id #uuid "1bca9c9f-347e-50cd-983a-012520b04ec9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256213} {:answer/id #uuid "7182fa70-cf00-5a72-8698-deb11fabc8da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256214} {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} {:answer/id #uuid "4b12d860-258e-5359-827c-56ef56e1e69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be86f2e5-0b3d-52c0-a00f-2a4b04f18b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256215} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4715576-2b79-520b-9527-45c19ddc2f36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256211}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9834bdc8-d968-5825-adae-a20e0fb4ec63" :question/math-academy-id "q-119948" :question/problem "Simplify $\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10}) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "259af117-dceb-5d92-abb6-78ee4dbe45b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256219} {:answer/id #uuid "13501dc1-91f1-50aa-88fa-312ee8cdac06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256220} {:answer/id #uuid "3b66245e-074c-59dd-920a-92c576ce02f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256221} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a16802-76c8-5290-bef6-7bae397c680b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256222} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7a02d4-9163-5c52-a72c-66c7ebcf2fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "259af117-dceb-5d92-abb6-78ee4dbe45b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256219} :answer-field/id #uuid "abbeaaab-d37e-5373-92d7-54f74146b9f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256218}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b7e01ede-c189-5723-8722-daa6f3b0ddd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-120018" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ in the denominator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72b7fefd-5832-5a10-88fe-941167df7f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256226} {:answer/id #uuid "7507e855-4c12-51a7-9a9f-ae6f5e8b92e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256227} {:answer/id #uuid "941450ca-b432-57e0-88da-4f3e57cded91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256228} {:answer/id #uuid "6a05b73c-5266-524e-942d-aa4fdaa77be4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256229} {:answer/id #uuid "b579223d-8d16-53c6-9211-cd05c4c8fd36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "941450ca-b432-57e0-88da-4f3e57cded91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256228} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce6d0c7-9a44-59bf-beba-79c56172cfc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256225}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2169c30-fb8b-5ed9-9ee8-c3820a8c3a72" :question/math-academy-id "q-120024" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can simplify the given expression by rewriting the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})$ in the numerator, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32741f4f-5f3b-54f4-9a54-99df8f2ed7eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256233} {:answer/id #uuid "edc29643-b617-541c-856c-135676894e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256234} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc00b94-761f-50d8-b824-5367d0294851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256235} {:answer/id #uuid "126557c4-03cb-5df0-96b8-44428932ce41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256236} {:answer/id #uuid "bc35480c-9e68-5723-bb86-f232d0d85fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edc29643-b617-541c-856c-135676894e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256234} :answer-field/id #uuid "c632c235-f581-5701-a287-08e8082006b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256232}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2628c4f1-9365-518c-ad53-f5432ebf8a51" :question/math-academy-id "q-120030" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{140}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity in the form ${cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}=1-{sin}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘}}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2(1-{sin}^{2}⁡{70}^{∘})}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})\\cancel{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘})}}{\\cancel{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =2(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c598e3d-8ec0-5060-9c46-6604a72abcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256240} {:answer/id #uuid "f7f8f370-5c53-58d5-b28a-3312eb2ef750" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256241} {:answer/id #uuid "448580ff-e38e-57bf-9ca3-e7ce3176cf72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256242} {:answer/id #uuid "8f36e0c4-2cb1-5785-bcd9-afae4aaefa72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256243} {:answer/id #uuid "42f6c4eb-a87f-58bf-aef3-28ceb4c29ea9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c598e3d-8ec0-5060-9c46-6604a72abcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256240} :answer-field/id #uuid "e283ba02-233b-5f63-8318-1d0a3156c7ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256239}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "081c95ae-81cb-52c0-9684-47a33bf79aa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120058" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256245 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c52b5511-9b22-51d4-abcb-71de31ff9e94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256247} {:answer/id #uuid "d22e0927-d5be-58cd-a430-70149387cadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256248} {:answer/id #uuid "9f7e2225-e489-516d-97ad-6ed329e4d6ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256249} {:answer/id #uuid "5999ac75-6f23-5ab3-a5d3-56f8903910ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256250} {:answer/id #uuid "bc1e05b2-a95b-57dc-b431-2f45bddc475e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc1e05b2-a95b-57dc-b431-2f45bddc475e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256251} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3a0efb4-4bda-530b-b7e0-1c9f52df549b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256246}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e65bef42-c4ca-5ef8-8e09-232966b68e6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-24645" :question/problem "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =2[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4bffe8b-3637-547c-99be-c2ee069ca61c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256254} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b9e4e0-fa4d-5e47-b517-e31db15c125f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256255} {:answer/id #uuid "ed742626-ab3e-5908-9345-2200a481d3f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256256} {:answer/id #uuid "7b163501-27d4-56be-b447-5a3ccfd8d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256257} {:answer/id #uuid "0446b95c-c2af-560d-abd1-109cb4fc118a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b163501-27d4-56be-b447-5a3ccfd8d07a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256257} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bb793c7-2ed0-5340-b770-f69725fc53fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256253}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04ad99db-b562-50ab-884b-fce6f7ff1c92" :question/math-academy-id "q-24647" :question/problem "Express $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "900df914-20ff-5505-b0f6-e326c001dea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256261} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6db32f-f11a-52e4-b56d-01a2b5ea4461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256262} {:answer/id #uuid "d46f1e43-7407-5544-8349-047af93bae8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256263} {:answer/id #uuid "3c57098c-ca4d-5089-8705-33bb4cd019fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256264} {:answer/id #uuid "2c77db3a-1aa4-539f-a780-ce22a2aaacb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "900df914-20ff-5505-b0f6-e326c001dea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256261} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e25409f-82af-5dfd-aae5-d19fca9342ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256260}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01561bb9-e823-5e9c-a4a2-3c80ab23970f" :question/math-academy-id "q-26907" :question/problem "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})]+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={105}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({210}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256266 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2580912-9437-58b6-aa92-b2bc4ba5d863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256268} {:answer/id #uuid "b8f7c825-7707-587d-8e45-1b9720663027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8f7c825-7707-587d-8e45-1b9720663027" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256269} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ae0d78-4bdd-5308-93fd-56a84c536b1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256267}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67832bb6-04a4-5dd5-a172-5c2d6c2063e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-327247" :question/problem "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2}.$\n\n${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})]+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's recall the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}))}^{2}=1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0e0681e-e415-58e5-bbfa-fab3a58a6398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0e0681e-e415-58e5-bbfa-fab3a58a6398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256272} :answer-field/id #uuid "3511f9b5-075c-5b03-891e-874ccc91a604" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256271}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b7ad8a7a-7fe3-5da1-8b56-916c39195e84" :question/math-academy-id "q-327277" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{8})}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256273 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41c89a54-fb37-5e7f-b93d-ebbdffe60694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256275} {:answer/id #uuid "75fef84a-4659-5182-9dc8-65882bb13b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41c89a54-fb37-5e7f-b93d-ebbdffe60694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256275} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b960d8-b823-521f-ba0a-f080d7d65c62" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256274}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "62770764-8176-56e9-8c60-1a1dcb94a9d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-327716" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a4ec08-4df2-504b-8bb2-165aa83be092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a4ec08-4df2-504b-8bb2-165aa83be092" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256279} :answer-field/id #uuid "341f39aa-6a81-5083-8264-e503b649bf89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256278}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c3ab403-d373-50aa-ab7d-cad9629d8aab" :question/math-academy-id "q-327763" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}).$\n\n$14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{8}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8}) & =7\\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{8})) \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256280 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bed365c5-0288-5a0b-af12-adb975de962b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bed365c5-0288-5a0b-af12-adb975de962b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256282} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfc2e1ef-318e-5dbb-b289-b4c8ac01a20b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256281}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d196384f-4e56-525b-b52f-9a047afd0095" :question/math-academy-id "q-364639" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula Multiple Times"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a3cbfb-4b25-5278-a653-b36ffcef4db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256285}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12a3cbfb-4b25-5278-a653-b36ffcef4db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256285} :answer-field/id #uuid "b189a8a4-4669-5bff-b037-1f9fc969ab66" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256284}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6aab47f3-0a6d-55dd-bbdd-19d0314c54b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-364640" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12})}{\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fad28e1-e45c-5970-8eb0-8e24b340d75e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256288} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d74f78-c9ff-5684-af61-e41710afdca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256289} {:answer/id #uuid "3e939cb2-579b-544f-8b16-15deac80b66d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256290} {:answer/id #uuid "836bf5df-0bbf-5254-8c3a-6f6a7038e6d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256291} {:answer/id #uuid "a478a4fb-46f9-585a-9631-09fb14d62234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "836bf5df-0bbf-5254-8c3a-6f6a7038e6d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256291} :answer-field/id #uuid "84fc3269-afd2-5a72-b68d-2ee261077eb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256287}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d175d08f-2189-55e6-be14-13052ef393af" :question/math-academy-id "q-65609" :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{10})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}).\n$$\n\nRewriting the given expression using the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10})}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{10}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f9683d9-05b9-5a42-9f81-0170a15dfac1" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Ratios"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e06a6935-d6a1-508b-a1de-8ad379c7be1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256295} {:answer/id #uuid "3f57ccc9-af0c-58a8-bbed-8535d504a79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256296} {:answer/id #uuid "38254b3a-cf05-5cb5-89c8-4108d68efea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256297} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d661f7-6693-5159-90b5-a9efbee4ec3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256298} {:answer/id #uuid "4abe4586-6e46-5d81-b73e-4ffcb8a5d8ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡{64}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9d661f7-6693-5159-90b5-a9efbee4ec3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256298} :answer-field/id #uuid "f482b4e5-ec7e-56b4-9872-96f676280438" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256294}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c12914c-6180-54b3-b700-f4f558927e76" :question/math-academy-id "q-65615" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{64}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={32}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {32}^{∘})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{64}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{64}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{32}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{32}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "143766e0-0ef5-5caf-b699-d394d4a707e9" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Products"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c2ebd8-fdbf-5b5b-8ba1-8fc5fd77a0e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256302} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1196b0-4c7c-5880-9caf-53995ca6623b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256303} {:answer/id #uuid "62346b99-48f0-5873-bfe4-a384b2655b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256304} {:answer/id #uuid "30b3b57a-350b-57aa-9671-d921d8ac88f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{14})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256305} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb68c40-7670-55f8-9bb2-511ad8765fcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{7})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62346b99-48f0-5873-bfe4-a384b2655b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operato